# Git Traceability

Git work associated with an OpenSpec change in this repository's OpenSpec workspace must be attributable to that change. A reader of the commit must be able to identify the change.

A single commit must not contain work that belongs to more than one OpenSpec change.

Git history is not the specification. OpenSpec remains the requirement contract. If this repository has no OpenSpec workspace yet, still do not treat commit messages as the specification.

Committing propose, apply, sync, or archive work for a change is allowed when that commit is attributable to that change. Not every commit must name a change.

This file reminds that existing contract. OpenSpec specifications remain the source of truth.

Authoritative methodology (page titles, not this file): Workflow system. Documentation root is `docs/` here and `docs/sdd-framework/` after copy/pin of the SDD Framework baseline.
